               },
               "body" : {
                  "content" : [
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Mark fixed in 3.0d1 - enuf done that we can do that. We DONT actaulyl store as UTF8 cuz they are variable sized and make indexing hard. But we check ‘length’ of max length character - usaulyl 1 for ascii (and will soonbe done for any where codepoint < 255) - and store those directly as bytes. And thats the main optimization. also do/will do a little more - if fits in 2 bytes - will also store then in just two. Key is not assumign anywhere Character* convertable to/from wchar_t* - so this mostly should help on unix performance, and only a bit for window.s",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
                  ],
                  "type" : "doc",
                  "version" : 1
               },
               "created" : "2023-01-07T17:03:01.794-0500",
               "id" : "16348",
